    {
      "id": "abc-1",
      "name": "Special Abilities",
      "desc": "Class Benefits:\n• Priest Spells\n\nClass Hinderances:\n• None\n\nChrom, the God of Creation and Craft\n• Turn Undead\n• Burn for: Exchange a memorized spell for a cure spell of the same level\n• Experienced: Use which ever is better, Wis or Int, for craft skills\n• Major Domains: See Spells Sheet\n• Minor Domains: See Spells Sheet\n\nKit Benefits:\n• Free Craft Proficiency: Player Choice (Weaponsmith)\n• Bonus Proficiencies: Endurance, Religion\n\nKit Hinderances:\n• None.",
      "url": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "abc-2",
      "name": "Racial Abilities",
      "desc": "Racial Abilities: Con +1, Cha -1, Size: Small, Speed 6, Night Vision\n\nConstitute: +4 Bonus to Save vs Poison\n\nAntimagical:\n+4 Bonus to Save vs Rods, Staves, Wands, and Spells\nIf a magical item is not specifically created for the dwarf's class, there is a 20% chance of malfunction when used. Dwarves have learned to master some magical items. Weapons, shields, armor, gauntlets, and girdles always work. Dwarf priests and warrior/priests may use clerical items without malfunction. Dwarves also recognize cursed magical items that malfunction in their hands. They may dispose of malfunctioning items.\n\nEnemy of my people: +1 bonus to attack orcs, half-orcs, goblins, and hobgoblins.\n\nUnderground Sense:\nDetect grade or slope in passage, 1-5 on a d6\nDetect new tunnel/passage construction, 1-5 on a d6\nDetect sliding/shifting walls or rooms, 1-4 on a d6\nDetect stonework traps, pits, and deadfalls, 1-3 on a d6\nEstimate approximate depth underground, 1-3 on a d6",
      "url": ""
    }
  ],
